  "semantics": [
    "Each request uses fresh native account authority; cookies and forged internal owner headers do not grant file access. Ownership and readiness are checked before buffering and again at driver dispatch.",
    "Uploads check the complete length and SHA256 before effects. Create-only identical retries succeed; conflicts return412. Explicit overwrite publishes a new mode0600 inode by atomic rename and flushes both file and directory. An identical retry keeps existing permissions.",
    "The helper pins a regular inode before I/O, takes a read lease, bounds the copy, checks metadata and lease afterward, and returns409 on a changing file. Symlinks, mount crossings, devices, sockets, directories, and FIFOs are refused.",
    "openat2 and Landlock ABI2 confine paths and directory moves. The helper never truncates existing inodes; O_TRUNC is rejected explicitly. ABI3 adds kernel truncation restrictions. There is no unrestricted fallback.",
    "Two stalled uploads exhaust the two slots before any provider effect; a third transfer returns429. A raw over-limit request is refused before its body is sent.",
    "A lost write reply is uncertain rather than successful; read and compare the hash before retrying. A checked complete download is buffered within the bound before HTTP success begins.",
    "Stopped or starting computers return409; deleted or missing computers return404. Transfers never wake or recreate one. Existing public files and legacy driver/conformance paths remain separate and passing."
  ],
  "live_findings": [
    {
      "finding": "Supported Boat guest mounts /run noexec; executing there failed126. Its6.1.0-53-cloud-amd64 kernel predates the initial ABI3 requirement; direct helper returned18.",
      "correction": "Root-owned executable directory under /var/lib, removed after every transfer; ABI2 REFER policy with only new-inode writes and explicit O_TRUNC refusal. Forced-ABI2 race and hardlink checks passed."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Cloud Run rejects empty PUT without a length before the application.",
      "negative_control": {
        "record": "cmp_373e220a2a20965c005b, already deleted and owned by the dedicated staging account",
        "missing_length": 411,
        "explicit_zero": 404,
        "effects": "none"
      },
      "correction": "Web binary proxy sends Content-Length0 for empty PUT. Mock-provider and public empty upload/download checks cover it."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Early oversized-body refusal reset the Cloud Run HTTP/1 connection and hid413.",
      "correction": "Send413 headers and JSON immediately, then keep the response stream open while discarding chunks without buffering, bounded to32MiB/60seconds. Hold the existing transfer slot until completion or disconnect. Full-body, raw headers, two stalled slots, and disconnect regression checks pass."
    }
  ],
